# Port PR #75624: Add Node.js Runtime Support for Middleware

## PR Description

**Title:** Port middleware nodejs runtime support from upstream #75624

**Body:**

This PR ports the core changes from upstream [vercel/next.js#75624](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/75624) ("Add nodejs runtime support for middleware") into our fork.

### Summary of Changes

1. **Unconditional runtime resolution** (`get-page-static-info.ts`): `getPagesPageStaticInfo` now unconditionally resolves `config.runtime ?? config.config?.runtime` instead of only resolving when `isEdgeRuntime` was true or `getServerSideProps`/`getStaticProps` were present. This allows middleware to declare `runtime: 'nodejs'`.

2. **Middleware dispatch in `runDependingOnPageType`** (`entries.ts`): The `isMiddlewareFile` branch now checks `pageRuntime` — if `'nodejs'`, dispatches to `onServer()`; otherwise dispatches to `onEdgeServer()`. All existing API route and page logic is untouched.

3. **Guard and entry point creation in `createEntrypoints`** (`entries.ts`): When middleware declares `runtime: 'nodejs'` but `config.experimental.nodeMiddleware` is disabled, a warning is logged and `pageRuntime` falls back to `'edge'`. When the flag is enabled (or runtime is not `'nodejs'`), a new `else if (isMiddlewareFile(page))` branch creates the edge server entry via `getEdgeServerEntry`.

4. **Unit tests**: Three scenarios covering nodejs+flag enabled, nodejs+flag disabled (fallback), and no explicit runtime (default edge).

### Notes
- Our fork uses `config.experimental.nodeMiddleware` (disabled by default). This differs from upstream's default — a changeset is included.
- Rin's `middleware-resolver.ts` was reviewed; no conflicts found with these entry-point changes (see review notes below).
- The truncated `prefe` parameter from the upstream diff is resolved to `prefetch: false`.

---

## Commit Message

```
Port middleware nodejs runtime support from upstream #75624

Port the core changes from vercel/next.js#75624 ("Add nodejs runtime
support for middleware") into our fork.

Changes:
- get-page-static-info.ts: Resolve runtime unconditionally so middleware
  can declare runtime: 'nodejs' without being forced to edge.
- entries.ts: Dispatch middleware to Node.js server when pageRuntime is
  'nodejs'; warn and fall back to edge when experimental.nodeMiddleware
  flag is disabled.
- Add unit tests for the three middleware runtime dispatch scenarios.

Our fork requires experimental.nodeMiddleware to be explicitly enabled;
a warning is logged if middleware requests nodejs runtime without the
flag.

Refs: https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/75624
Refs: https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/71727
Refs: https://github.com/vercel/next.js/discussions/46722
